## Datatype: It helps to specify what type of data stored in the variable

## Based on the size of data we have 2 types

##1. Single value Datatype: We will store single value wrt one variable

    ## There are 2 types in SVD
    
        ##1. Numeric
        
            ## There are 3 types
            
                ## Integer: 
                        ##1. These are real number without decimals
                        ##2. we can have +ve or -ve 
                        ##3. The default value of integer is 0
        
        
a = 100
print(type(a))      ## type(): It is an inbuilt function, which helps to determine the type of value stored in the variable

a = -100
print(type(a))
print(type(900))

print(type(0))

                ## Float:
                        ##1. These are the real numbers with decimals
                        ##2. +ve or -ve float value
                        ##3. The default value of float is 0.0


b = 2.22
print(type(b))

print(type(-9.999))

print(type(0.0))

                ##3. complex:
                        ##1. The complex numbers are represented as a+/-bj
                        ##2. The value for a and b can either be int or float
                        ##3. The default value is 0j
                        
c = 2 +9j
print(type(c))


c = 2 +9.8j
print(type(c))

c = 2.8 +9.8j
print(type(c))

c = -2 +9.8j
print(type(c))

c = -2 - 9.8j
print(type(c))

print(c)

# c = -2 - 9.8i
# print(type(c))

c = -2 - 9.8J
print(type(c))
print(c)

## We can't use can alphabets in the imaginary part of complex number except J/j
## If we have "j" it stores as is suppose if we have "J" internally it converts to lower case

print(type(0j))

        ##2. Boolean
                    ## It has 2 values: True and False
                        # These values are used in 2cases
                            ##1. These are used as value to the variable
                            ##2. These are used as resultant to check the condition
                            
a, b = True, False
print(type(a), type(b))

print(11 > 4)
print(11 < 2)


